-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"b71b5f8c-8f26-4b3f-99bf-ad99e4c6733c\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"custom_regex_-D7xQ0kK-n\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"regex\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-11T03:14:49.695Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-10T12:52:33.738Z\", \"displayName\": \"Critical Violation Monitor\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"7e05f2a3-26c4-4536-afbe-ca7b024a145c\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"suggested-Os9kF1jX\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"regex\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-12T06:30:20.411Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-10T12:52:06.321Z\", \"displayName\": \"High Latency LLM Monitor\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"0ea4071a-c72a-409c-8e51-bdbc4a1e3ab1\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"suggested-axh1pWdA\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"conditional\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-12T06:30:08.426Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-10T07:57:33.088Z\", \"displayName\": \"Critical safety stop\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"419644ba-6cd5-4a66-8a84-10528e4467c0\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"custom_regex_Ib4qy_Fx3r\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"regex\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-10T07:57:44.336Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-10T07:57:29.915Z\", \"displayName\": \"Oath violation\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"195c2e97-38be-4e54-8ebc-e97cdf57ab3c\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"custom_regex_mGhjUZTh27\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"regex\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-10T07:57:42.231Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-10T03:14:51.006Z\", \"displayName\": \"Expensive LLM Call\", \"groupId\": \"b61657e3-9d41-47cc-b1a8-ca65\r\ndocs/TOOLS.md:46:| [HR-006](../evidence/hardening/HR-006.md) | Found in the frames of the first story video, not by a check | New promise `image_no_text` |\ndocs/TOOLS.md:73:- **`entire why`** on `src/storybound/oath/catalog.py` ties 18 lines to the checkpoint of the `image_no_text` change; on `pipeline.py` it ties lines to the HR-002 ablation switch.\ndocs/TOOLS.md:156:Through the MCP with the project key (reads need no login): analytics views (kpis, cost, errors, time, tools, detections, waste, workflows), the detection list and trends, the triage list, trace search and trace context. Result in [research/neatlogs-incident-review.md](research/neatlogs-incident-review.md) (a 135-line review by a subagent, checked against the ledger): 2,095 traces, 110 error traces of which 58 of the 62 matched to the ledger still shipped (trace status \"error\" means a span errored, not that the story failed); the 87 s Gemini stall back in bursts; 9 of 13 critical safety stops were false positives on \"hurt/fight\" (all before HR-004) and 4 intended; two detections had never fired; no alert could notify anyone; model mix and tool error rates (`illustrate` failed 17 of 66 calls). Fixed or acted on in [HR-011](../evidence/hardening/HR-011.md): hedged retry for the stall, tiering of \"ignore all\", a quiz detection on GUARDRAIL spans, `STORYBOUND_TAGS`; the alerts were then retuned after the builder's sign-in (`evidence/neatlogs/20261011-alert-retune-results.json`): oath violation 40 an hour (it fired on nearly every story at 3), slow story p95 450 s, expensive story $0.10 on measured text cost, a new rule on the corrected quiz detection, and the blind \"Quiz questions dropped\" rule disabled. **Email delivery is on for all seven rules** and a real test alert was queued (`evidence/neatlogs/20261011-alert-email-results.json`). Delivery goes to each neatlogs user's own account email through their notification preferences (per user, not a typed address); no custom address can be set on a rule, and a webhook is the only way to reach another place. The three old triage cards were then handled through the MCP with the neatlogs team email (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/triage_actions.json`): the PII card dismissed with a note (neatlogs's own redaction), the \"hurts\" card resolved (HR-004, HR-011), the latency card kept in progress until a real stall shows the hedge in traces. Still open: the picture-words detection and the orphan traces (HR-011 records what was tried: picture-verdict spans are missing from the story's trace, and a minimal thread-pool test attached fine).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cee00403-4803-4f84-af6f-ab6b50112a33","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:00:06.232Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Commands:\n  backfill [options] <detection-id>             explicitly rescore a bounded historical trace set\n  backfills                                     historical backfill jobs\n  preview [options]\n  generate [options]\n  suggestions-run [options]\n  suggestions-run-status <run-id>\n  suggestions-run-cancel [options] <run-id>\n  suggestions-list [options]\n  suggestion-accept [options] <suggestion-id>\n  suggestion-dismiss [options] <suggestion-id>\n  list [options]\n  get <detection-id>\n  create [options]\n  update [options] <detection-id>\n  enable [options] <detection-id>\n  disable [options] <detection-id>\n  delete [options] <detection-id>\n  history [options] <detection-id>\n  hits [options] <detection-id>\n  trends [options] <detection-id>\n  help [command]                                display help for command\n{\"detections\": [{\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-11T08:01:20.073Z\", \"displayName\": \"Quiz promise broken (GUARDRAIL span)\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"Negative\", \"id\": \"23c770b3-5257-4627-8524-dea06b741b91\", \"isActive\": true, \"slug\": \"custom_regex_J2eXINRZFx\", \"threshold\": 0.5, \"type\": \"regex\", \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-11T08:02:35.116Z\"}, {\"createdAt\": \"2026-10-11T03:12:41.971Z\", \"displayName\": \"Quiz question failed a promise\", \"groupId\": \"dd23563a-adba-4248-b9c6-ff1990b1cb69\", \"groupName\": \"N